{{!-- Waffen: reserved layout, no data behind it yet.

The system has no `weapon` item type — item, feature, spell and armor are the
four in `template.json` — and no readiness state, so there is nothing to list
here and nothing to roll. The block ships as the empty column headers plus a
hint saying so, rather than being left out: the Basics tab's right column is
laid out around three blocks, and an absent third one would silently change the
column's proportions the moment weapons land.

Do not fill this in from `inventory` — a carried item is not a readied weapon,
and conflating the two is exactly the design question that is still open. --}}
<div class='weapons-block card'>

  <div class='weapons-header'>
    <span class='weapons-title'>{{localize 'TNO.Weapons.Title'}}</span>
    <span class='weapons-pending' title='{{localize "TNO.Weapons.PendingHint"}}'>
      {{localize 'TNO.Weapons.Pending'}}
    </span>
  </div>

  <div class='weapons-table'>
    <div class='weapons-row weapons-columns'>
      <span class='weapon-name'>{{localize 'TNO.Weapons.Name'}}</span>
      <span class='weapon-cell'>{{localize 'TNO.Weapons.Dice'}}</span>
      <span class='weapon-cell'>{{localize 'TNO.Weapons.Damage'}}</span>
      <span class='weapon-cell'>{{localize 'TNO.Weapons.Range'}}</span>
    </div>
    <p class='weapons-empty'>{{localize 'TNO.Weapons.EmptyHint'}}</p>
  </div>

</div>
